  "advancements.potato_s_t.titanium_armor.title": "Titanium Alloy Suit",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.titanium_armor.description": "You need this before you can have the vibranium set",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.star_steel_tools.title": "A Collector's Habit",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.star_steel_tools.description": "Obtain a full set of Star Steel tools",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.star_steel_slash.title": "Starlight Slash",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.star_steel_slash.description": "When can we summon the Starlight Reaper?",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.star_chart_tome.title": "Your Subject Observes the Heavens",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.star_chart_tome.description": "All you see is illusion, yet this is the first step toward a new world...",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.title": "Large Diesel Generator",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.description": "Controller, two Low Generators, a Combustion Chamber and a Fluid Pump in 3x5x2, 30 blocks. 1 mB of diesel per tick makes 7200 FE",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.silver_wire.title": "Silver Wire",
  "advancements.potato_s_t.silver_wire.description": "The best heat and electricity conductor in nature",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.star_chart.1": "Right-click to cycle the Overworld skybox (sneak-right-click to go back)",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.star_chart.2": "Cycles through four star charts and the vanilla sky; the choice is stored in the book",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.star_chart.3": "Only you see it - the ignorant will never understand art",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.starfall_pendant.1": "Right-click: call a meteor down on your position. It falls from y=200 after 30 s",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.starfall_pendant.2": "Right-click again within the first 10 s to cancel; after that it is locked and everyone sees the countdown and your coordinates",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.starfall_pendant.3": "Impact: an explosion of power 7-20 plus a spray of raw ores - the higher the power, the better and the more",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.starfall_pendant.4": "· 7-12: nothing but scrap raw iron / raw copper · 13+: any raw ore · 15+: 3 extra raw vibranium",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.starfall_pendant.5": "4 uses in total; cannot be enchanted",
  "block.potato_s_t.diesel_generator_controller": "Diesel Generator Controller",
  "tooltip.potato_s_t.diesel_generator_controller": "How to lay out the Diesel Generator:\n1 Heat-Resistant Metal Block  2 Common Metal Block  3 Fluid Pump  4 Low-Tier Generator\n5 Combustion Chamber  6 Block of Copper  7 Copper Grate  8 Wiring Block  9 Diesel Generator Controller\nLayer 1 (bottom) | Layer 2\n1 3 1 | 2 1 2\n1 4 1 | 6 7 6\n1 5 1 | 6 7 6\n1 4 1 | 6 7 6\n1 9 1 | 2 8 2\nWith the controller's facing as the front, the machine runs 5 rows back and 2 layers up - not a single cell less.\nCopper blocks and grates: any oxidation level, waxed or not (all 16 count).\nOnce complete, the Wiring Block directly above the controller becomes a port (same texture, drops back as a Wiring Block) - and that is the only place power comes out.\nGUI: an 8000 mB diesel tank and a status lamp; 1 mB of diesel per tick makes 7200 FE; a redstone signal halts it.\nGetting diesel in: hook up a pump (controller or port), or right-click the controller with a Diesel Bucket or an oil bucket holding diesel.\n⚠ The Fluid Pump / two Low-Tier Generators / Combustion Chamber inside stay as they are - they are not consumed.",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.status.running": "Generating",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.status.disabled": "Halted (redstone signal)",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.status.empty": "Diesel tank is empty: pump it in, or right-click with a diesel bucket",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.status.output_full": "Power has nowhere to go",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.status.no_structure": "Structure incomplete: hold Shift for the blueprint (the missing cells are printed in chat)",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.invalid": "Gap in the structure: layer %s, row %s, column %s should be %s, but it is %s (at %s %s %s)",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.pour.empty": "The container in your hand is empty",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.pour.rejected": "Cannot pour in: %s (this machine only burns diesel)",
  "gui.potato_s_t.diesel_generator.pour.full": "The diesel tank cannot take it: the tank is full, or this whole bucket (1000 mB) does not fit",
  "block.potato_s_t.diesel_generator_port": "Diesel Generator Port",
  "item.potato_s_t.guide_book": "PotatoS&T Guide Book",
  "potato_s_t.guide.subtitle": "0.12 · From raw ore to a fallen star",
  "potato_s_t.guide.landing": "This book follows the mod version, and every step points at a recipe you can look up in JEI. Pick a chapter on the left — start with Getting Started.$(br2)Lost the book? One vanilla book plus one iron ingot crafts another.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.getting_started": "Getting Started",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.power": "Power",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.materials": "Materials",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.oil": "Oil and Chemistry",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.starfall": "Starfall",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.faq": "Troubleshooting",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.getting_started.desc": "Your first machine, your first production line, and the rules every machine shares.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.power.desc": "Wiring, generation and storage — plus how fluids and gases are moved.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.materials.desc": "How ore becomes dust, ingots and plates — plus the blast furnace, alloys and titanium.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.oil.desc": "Where crude oil comes from, how to build the distillation tower, and the four chemistry machines.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.starfall.desc": "Watch the sky, call down a meteor, and arm yourself with star steel and vibranium.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.category.faq.desc": "Machine not running, fluid not matching — read these two pages first.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.start": "Starting from Zero",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.start.p1": "The main line of this mod has five steps: crush raw ore into dust, smelt dust into ingots in the Electric Blast Furnace, press ingots into plates, open up power and chemistry, and finish with a fallen star.$(br2)Without dust you cannot do anything, so the very first thing to build is a Micro Crusher. It needs a steady supply of power — at the start, a Low Generator burning coal or charcoal is enough.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.start.p2": "Place the crusher in the middle of your workspace and leave one block in front of it to stand on. Then wire it up: build a Low Generator and bring the power over with terminals or cable spools (see the Power chapter).$(br2)Dust is the foundation of everything later on — crush every raw ore you find, and do not worry about having too much.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.rules": "How Machines Behave",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.rules.p1": "Every machine follows one iron rule: a redstone signal shuts it down, and its progress is kept. Want a switch? Put a lever or redstone line next to it.$(br2)A machine only accepts its own kind of input — put in the wrong thing and the interface tells you plainly what it refuses.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.rules.p2": "Right-click any machine with an empty hand while sneaking to get a slot-by-slot diagnosis: it tells you line by line which slot lacks what, which tank is empty, and whether power is missing.$(br2)The energy bar, fluid tanks, progress bar and status lamp in the interface are all live. If the lamp is red, read the diagnosis first and then fix that one thing.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.first_line": "Your First Line",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.getting_started.first_line.p1": "A complete starter line has four steps: raw ore into the Micro Crusher becomes dust, dust into the Electric Blast Furnace becomes an ingot, and an ingot into the Hydraulic Press becomes a plate.$(br2)Plates are a common part of nearly every machine, so press a batch whenever you run low. Ingots can also be used for crafting directly, so you do not have to press them all. Pressing bitumen takes 12 at a time, so do not feed it just a few.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.wiring": "Terminals and Cables",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.wiring.p1": "Terminals handle long-distance power transfer: right-click to place the first terminal and select it, then right-click a second one and the two are connected. If they are too far apart it refuses outright and tells you the limit.$(br2)The power inlet of a machine is the wiring block on its shell (on a formed multiblock that block turns into a port) — connect your terminals to those.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.wiring.p2": "Cable spools also connect terminals: copper and silver spools both reach 16 blocks and both have 32 durability, returning an empty spool when used up. The difference is throughput — copper carries 2048 FE/t, silver carries 16134 FE/t.$(br2)The power cable spool does not carry electricity but rotation, and it is how the Power Capturer pulls power in. The creative cable is for debugging; do not run a real production line on it.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.generation": "Three Ways to Make Power",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.generation.p1": "Low Generator: burns coal or charcoal to make power, and a redstone signal shuts it down. It is the easiest one to start with — a single unit is enough to run a Micro Crusher.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.generation.p2": "Solar Panel: generates only in daytime and peaks near noon; the block directly above must be air or clear glass. Panels placed side by side join into one array, sharing output and storage across the whole group.$(br2)Rain cuts it to 60 percent, a thunderstorm to 20 percent, and at night it makes nothing at all.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.generation.p3": "Need more power? Go the rotation route: the Power Capturer takes rotation from an adjacent source and the power cable spool carries it; then the Generator converts rotation into electricity at 2 FE/t per point.$(br2)Only with these three working together are you really in the industrial age.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.storage": "Storing Power: Lithium Batteries",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.storage.p1": "A single Lithium Battery stores 4M FE. Place batteries flush against each other as a full rectangular box and they merge into one multiblock whose capacity adds up — only the top face can transfer FE.$(br2)Allowed footprints are 2x2, 2x3, 3x3, 3x4, 4x4 and 5x5; 2x2 allows up to 6 layers, 2x3 / 3x3 / 3x4 up to 12 layers, and 4x4 / 5x5 up to 32 layers.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.storage.p2": "Batteries need components first: the Lithium Battery Plant takes four inputs (raw manganese or raw aluminium, nickel ingot or raw nickel, lithium carbonate, cobalt ingot or raw cobalt), plus sulfuric acid, and produces one Lithium Battery Component every 30 seconds.$(br2)This machine uses no power — it runs on chemistry. Lithium carbonate comes from crushing raw lithium into lithium concentrate and smelting that concentrate in the Electric Blast Furnace.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.fluids": "Moving Fluids and Gases",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.fluids.p1": "Liquids travel in Oil Buckets and gases in High Pressure Tanks, and the Filling Machine fills both. It holds five tanks of 5000 mB each, and one tank holds only one kind of fluid. Right-click the machine with a bucket or tank in hand to pour its contents into a tank.$(br2)Filling runs at 5 mB/t per tank, and every tank that is working draws 60 FE/t.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.fluids.p2": "To put machine fluid back into portable containers, use the Fluid Exchanger: a filled bucket or tank goes in the left slot, one empty bucket in the right, and it turns the empty bucket into a bucket of that fluid.$(br2)Fluids with no bucket form (crude oil, naphtha, LPG) are refused outright — for those, pump them out instead.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.power.fluids.p3": "Fluid Pump: the front face is the input and the back face is the output, and pipes only attach to those two. Right-click to open its interface and set the speed from 0 to 800 percent. The pump stores nothing itself and only sends fluid the target can accept.$(br2)Route gases through the pump as well — do not expect the Fluid Exchanger to handle tanks.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.ore_chain": "Ore and Material Chain",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.ore_chain.p1": "There are nine ores: aluminium, cobalt, nickel, silver, uranium, manganese, lithium, wolframite (for tungsten) and titanium — seven of them have deepslate variants.$(br2)The standard flow has three steps: raw ore into the Micro Crusher becomes dust, and dust into the Electric Blast Furnace becomes an ingot. A few of them (sand, raw aluminium, raw silver) can also be smelted in a vanilla furnace, but dust in the blast furnace yields more.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.ore_chain.p2": "Press ingots into plates with the Hydraulic Press: iron, copper, nickel, cobalt, silver, aluminium, steel plates and more. Plates are a common part of nearly every machine, so press a batch whenever you run short.$(br2)A redstone signal shuts the press down and keeps its progress.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.blast_alloy": "Blast Furnace, Alloys and Titanium",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.blast_alloy.p1": "The Electric Blast Furnace is a 3x3x3 multiblock assembled right on top of a vanilla blast furnace. It has 12 input slots and 32 output slots, each slot finishes in 10 seconds, and every item costs 800 FE.$(br2)Besides this mod's ore processing, anything a vanilla blast furnace can smelt works here too. Feed it dust for better yields than a vanilla furnace.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.blast_alloy.p2": "The Alloy Smelter Controller needs the four-layer, 58-block pattern (floor, three-high walls, and those two rows of heat-resistant metal on the roof), plus at least one wiring block on the shell, before it activates by itself.$(br2)Its interface has 5 input slots (ingots only), 3 output slots and 2 consume slots; it stores 32768 FE and takes power only through the port. Four recipes, all in JEI.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.blast_alloy.p3": "The titanium line: crush raw titanium into titanium dust, then smelt that dust in the Electric Blast Furnace for titanium ingots.$(br2)From there come the alloys: light titanium alloy, hard titanium alloy and stable metal blocks — the Acidic Reaction Chamber and lithium batteries both need them. The titanium alloy sword and pickaxe are made from light titanium alloy as well.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.salt": "Salt from the Sea",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.salt.p1": "The Salt Dryer only works in an ocean or salty river biome, between Y 0 and 64, with a water source block below it: passive drying yields one sea salt every 120 seconds.$(br2)Supply it with FE and it speeds up to one every 20 seconds. Sunlight is fine, but electricity is faster.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.materials.salt.p2": "Careful: sea salt dropped into water dissolves and vanishes, so do not fumble it near the shore.$(br2)The Salt Decomposer takes 64 sea salt, and after 40 seconds yields 1 sodium chloride; it returns the salt 60 percent of the time, and adds a random raw ore 5 percent of the time. Put sea salt in the Electrolyzer's electrolyte slot to also produce chlorine while splitting water (one extra salt per 500 mB of water).",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.crude": "Where Crude Oil Comes From",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.crude.p1": "Oil fields exist both on land and under the sea. Right-click the block of an oil field with an empty Oil Bucket to scoop up one bucket of crude — an empty bucket does not count.$(br2)For volume you need the Oil Pump: it only runs in an ocean oil field biome and stops entirely anywhere else.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.crude.p2": "Hang a chain straight down from the machine and keep it under water; n is the number of waterlogged chain blocks. It draws 8n squared plus 80n FE/t, produces 10n mB/s, and has a 25-bucket tank.$(br2)Every 25 to 80 buckets pumped, the ocean oil field across the 10x10 chunk area around the machine turns into ordinary ocean. Those 100 chunks include the machine itself, so after one drawdown, move it to where oil remains.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.distillation": "The Distillation Tower",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.distillation.p1": "The Distillation Controller recognises a 4x4x7 tower of seven layers: layers 1 and 2 have common metal blocks at the four corners; layers 3 and 5 have common metal at the corners, heat-resistant metal along the edges, and a 2x2 of heaters in the middle; layers 4 and 6 are a ring of heat-resistant metal; layer 7 is solid common metal. Cells drawn empty on the plan must be air.$(br2)The controller counts towers within 32x32x10 around itself, up to four of them.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.distillation.p2": "The Distillation Operator is the part that actually works: each tower holds 12 buckets of crude oil and 2.5 buckets of every product, and a redstone signal starts it.$(br2)One tower splits crude oil five ways: diesel, gasoline, naphtha, LPG and bitumen. More towers mean more throughput and more tank space.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.chemistry": "The Four Chemistry Machines",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.chemistry.p1": "Combustion Chamber: put any vanilla furnace fuel in the fuel slot (lava bucket 10 seconds, diesel or gasoline bucket 30 seconds, anything else 3 seconds); one fuel plus 10 mB of oxygen starts a reaction, and while it runs it feeds 800 rotation per tick to a Power Capturer (1200 for diesel, 1000 for gasoline).$(br2)The oxygen tank only takes input and the carbon dioxide and water tanks only give output — pipe them.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.chemistry.p2": "The Air Separator draws 200 FE/t and produces nitrogen and oxygen — its feedstock is air, which never runs out.$(br2)The Ammonia Synthesis Chamber needs three things: nitrogen and hydrogen in its input tanks, plus one iron dust as a catalyst that is not consumed. The ammonia it makes is the feedstock for nitric acid.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.chemistry.p3": "Hydrodesulfurization Chamber: 16 bitumen plus 1000 mB of hydrogen per batch yields sulfur — the feedstock for sulfuric acid. This machine uses no electricity; it runs on chemistry.$(br2)The Acidic Reaction Chamber draws 500 FE/t and has four recipes in JEI: carbonic, nitric, sulfuric and hydrochloric acid.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.diesel_gen": "The Large Diesel Generator",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.diesel_gen.p1": "The Large Diesel Generator is a 3x5x2 multiblock of 30 blocks: with the controller facing you, build 5 rows back and 2 layers up, and not a single block may be missing.$(br2)The copper blocks and copper grates inside are accepted at any oxidation stage, waxed or not — all 16 variants work. Once complete, the wiring block directly above the controller turns into the port — and power leaves only from there.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.oil.diesel_gen.p2": "Its interface is just an 8000 mB diesel tank and a working lamp: it burns 1 mB of diesel per tick for 7200 FE, and a redstone signal stops it.$(br2)Diesel can be pumped in, or poured by right-clicking the controller with a diesel bucket. The fluid pump, the two low generators and the combustion chamber inside stay their own blocks after assembly — they are not consumed.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.starfall.sky_and_star": "Star Chart and Starfall Pendant",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.starfall.sky_and_star.p1": "The Star Chart Tome cycles the overworld skybox on right-click, and sneak-right-click steps back; four star charts rotate with the vanilla sky.$(br2)The setting is stored on the book itself and is visible only to you — everyone else on the server still sees the vanilla sky. Want stars? Just look up.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.starfall.sky_and_star.p2": "Right-click the Starfall Pendant to throw it: 30 seconds later a meteor comes down from y 200, and you can cancel within the first 10 seconds by right-clicking again. After that it locks, and the whole server sees the countdown and coordinates.$(br2)Impact is a blast of power 7 to 20 that scatters raw ore: 7 to 12 gives only raw iron and raw copper, 13 and up gives every raw ore, and 15 and up adds 3 raw vibranium. It has 4 durability and cannot be enchanted.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.starfall.star_steel": "Star Steel and Vibranium",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.starfall.star_steel.p1": "Star Steel armour keeps time with the night: when darkness falls each piece gains Resistance I and stops wearing out, and with all four resonating they never wear out in the End at all.$(br2)It also finds you a block to stand on within 20x20, catching you first and erasing the fall after; if there is nothing at all, it swaps places with a nearby creature.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.starfall.star_steel.p2": "Star Steel Sword with Shift and right-click: spend 100 durability to send out an 8-block slash of starlight that pierces every enemy along the way for 12 damage each and lights them for 5 seconds. The axe works the same way, releasing a 6-block-wide shockwave that fells logs.$(br2)Vibranium is the other path: the full set has unlimited durability, permanent Resistance I, immunity to fall and projectile damage, half blast damage, and immunity to all knockback; and every hit taken has a 10 percent chance of being returned as it was.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.faq.machine": "Machine Not Running?",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.faq.machine.p1": "Check in this order: first, is a redstone signal reaching it — if so, it stops; second, does the multiblock shell have a wiring block, because without power it will not work; third, structural gaps — right-click the controller and it prints the coordinates of the missing block to chat; fourth, empty-handed sneak right-click for a slot-by-slot diagnosis that says exactly what is missing.$(br2)Full tanks, a blocked output slot, or a missing catalyst also stop a machine, and the interface says which.",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.faq.fluid": "Fluid Mismatch?",
  "potato_s_t.guide.entry.faq.fluid.p1": "It is usually one of three things: one tank holds only one fluid, so anything else must be emptied first; crude oil, naphtha and LPG have no bucket form, so the Fluid Exchanger refuses them and only a pump can move them; and gases belong in High Pressure Tanks and pumps.$(br2)One more: a machine's tanks are usually output-only or input-only, so read the tooltip before you attach a pipe.",
  "message.potato_s_t.guide_book.received": "You received a PotatoS&T Guide Book: right-click to open it. If you lose it, craft a new one from a book and an iron ingot."
}
